<!-- snippets/jc-buybox-head.liquid -->
{% comment %}
  Top of the PDP buy column: eyebrow, title, one-line flavor description,
  certification chips, and the per-product bullets.

  Replaces what used to open the column — a "PREMIUM INGREDIENTS" badge pill and
  a five-item checklist identical on all five flavors — with the two things that
  differ per product: what this one tastes like, and what it is certified as.

  Every string is parsed from live product data by jc-product-facts.liquid. No
  chip list is written down here: Blue carries a Non-GMO mark and Black does
  not, and hardcoding either set would print a claim the other product cannot
  make.

  Accepts:
  - block: {object}

  Usage:
    {% render 'jc-buybox-head', block: block %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- capture jc_facts %}{% render 'jc-product-facts', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign f = jc_facts | strip | split: '§'
  assign jc_type = f[0] | strip
  assign jc_size = f[1] | strip
  assign jc_flavor = f[2] | strip
  assign jc_chips = f[3] | split: '¦'
  assign jc_caffeine = f[4] | strip
  assign jc_bullets = f[9] | split: '¦'

  # === EYEBROW ===
  # It used to be the descriptive half of the title, which on every product is
  # a verbatim repeat of the H1 directly beneath it — "HAZELNUT OAT MILK LATTE"
  # over "Jolene Blue: Hazelnut Oat Milk Latte" told the shopper nothing twice.
  # It now carries the two facts the title cannot: how much is in the can, and
  # how much caffeine. Both are already parsed off the nutrition panel.
  #
  # A product with no panel (the variety pack) falls back to the type label,
  # and only when the title does not already contain it — otherwise the eyebrow
  # is dropped rather than reinstated as a duplicate.
  assign jc_eyebrow = ''
  if jc_size != blank and jc_caffeine != blank
    assign jc_eyebrow = jc_size | append: ' · ' | append: jc_caffeine | append: ' caffeine'
  elsif jc_size != blank
    assign jc_eyebrow = jc_size
  elsif jc_caffeine != blank
    assign jc_eyebrow = jc_caffeine | append: ' caffeine'
  elsif jc_type != blank
    unless product.title contains jc_type
      assign jc_eyebrow = jc_type
    endunless
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Spacing comes from the column's own scale in attomik-custom.css, not from
  block.settings.spacing_top/bottom. Those settings live in
  templates/product.json and were set per block with no shared rhythm, which is
  what left a dead gap under the bullets and jammed STEP 1 against the price.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="jc-bb-head w-full"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {% if jc_eyebrow != blank %}
    <span class="jc-bb-eyebrow">{{ jc_eyebrow }}</span>
  {% endif %}

  <h1 class="jc-bb-title">{{ product.title }}</h1>

  {% if jc_flavor != blank %}
    <p class="jc-bb-flavor">{{ jc_flavor }}</p>
  {% endif %}

  {% if jc_chips.size > 0 %}
    <ul class="jc-bb-chips">
      {% for chip in jc_chips %}
        <li class="jc-bb-chip">{{ chip }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  {% endif %}

  {%- comment -%}
    Bullets sit WITH the chips, not instead of them. The chips are the same on
    every flavor — they prove trust but do not sell this particular can — so the
    per-product highlights carry the flavor argument underneath. Entries that
    only restate a chip are dropped upstream in jc-product-facts.liquid.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {% if jc_bullets.size > 0 %}
    <ul class="jc-bb-bullets">
      {% for bullet in jc_bullets %}
        <li class="jc-bb-bullet">{{ bullet }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  {% endif %}
</div>
